{:edb/db-before-t 1287 :edb/db-after-t 1288 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534600 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:05:05.965Z" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059422 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin 15^{∘}\\cos 15^{∘} &= \\sin (2 \\cdot 15^{∘}) = \\sin 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534600 false] [17592186059422 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059423 1100 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}$." 13194139534600 false] [17592186059423 1100 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}.$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059423 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})]\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$" 13194139534600 false] [17592186059423 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059424 1100 "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}$." 13194139534600 false] [17592186059424 1100 "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}.$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059424 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{\\sin 50^{∘}} &= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sec 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534600 false] [17592186059424 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡{25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059425 1100 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}$." 13194139534600 false] [17592186059425 1100 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}.$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059425 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{8}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 2\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}} = 3 \\left(\\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n$$" 13194139534600 false] [17592186059425 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by $\\dfrac 1 2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)} } = 3 \\left( \\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186059595 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298105 13194139534600 true] [17592186059596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298087 13194139534600 true] [17592186059596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298119 13194139534600 true] [17592186059597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298091 13194139534600 true] [17592186059597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298098 13194139534600 true] [17592186059598 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298079 13194139534600 true] [17592186059598 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298112 13194139534600 true] [17592186060162 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534600 true] [17592186060162 1100 "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186060162 1100 "What is $(\\sin (\\frac{π}{8}))/(\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}))$?" 13194139534600 false] [17592186060162 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186060170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534600 true] [17592186060170 1100 "Find the exact value of $(\\sin (\\frac{π}{12}) - \\cos (\\frac{π}{12}))^{2}$." 13194139534600 false] [17592186060170 1100 "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2}.$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186060170 1145 "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})]-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =1-(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186256278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298086 13194139534600 true] [17592186257401 1017 #edb/ref 17592186274364 13194139534600 false] [17592186257401 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298073 13194139534600 true] [17592186257401 1100 "$10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘})=$" 13194139534600 false] [17592186257401 1100 "$10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘})=$" 13194139534600 true] [17592186257401 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}({150}^{∘})} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534600 false] [17592186257401 1145 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\